[6] apply-quadratic-formula: On applique la formule : x = (−b ± √Δ) / (2a)
[7] simplify-solutions: On simplifie les solutions
[8] read-solutions: On conclut sur l’ensemble des solutions

========== LYCEE (summarized) ==========
[1] Équation du second degré
[2] On divise les deux membres par 3 (PGCD)
[3] On identifie les coefficients a, b et c
[4] On calcule le discriminant Δ = b² − 4ac
[5] Δ > 0 : deux solutions distinctes
[6] On applique la formule : x = (−b ± √Δ) / (2a)
[7] On simplifie les solutions
[8] Solutions

========== LYCEE (detailed) ==========
[1] Équation du second degré
    │ 3x^2 - 3x - 18 = 0
[2] On divise les deux membres par 3 (PGCD)
    │ \\begin{aligned}   3x^2 - 3x - 18 &= 0 \\\\   x^2 - x - 6 &= 0 \\end{aligned}
[3] On identifie les coefficients a, b et c
    │ a = 1, \\quad b = -1, \\quad c = -6
[4] On calcule le discriminant Δ = b² − 4ac
    │ \\Delta = b^2 - 4ac = \\left(-1\\right)^2 - 4 \\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\cdot \\left(-6\\right) = 25
[5] Δ > 0 : deux solutions distinctes
    │ x^2 - x - 6 = 0
[6] On applique la formule : x = (−b ± √Δ) / (2a)
    │ \\begin{aligned}   x &= \\dfrac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{\\Delta}}{2a} \\\\   &= \\dfrac{-\\left(-1\\right) \\pm \\sqrt{25}}{2 \\cdot \\left(1\\right)} \\end{aligned}
[7] On simplifie les solutions
    │ \\begin{aligned}   x_1 &= \\dfrac{1 - \\sqrt{25}}{2 1} = -2 \\\\
  x_2 &= \\dfrac{1 + \\sqrt{25}}{2 1} = 3 \\end{aligned}
[8] Solutions
    │ S = \\left\\{ -2 \\,;\\, 3 \\right\\}

========== SUPERIEUR (summarized) ==========
[1] Simplification (÷ 3)
[2] Coefficients a, b, c
[3] Discriminant : Δ > 0
[4] Formule du second degré
[5] Simplification
[6] Ensemble des solutions

========== SUPERIEUR (detailed) ==========
[1] Simplification (÷ 3)
    │ \\begin{aligned}   3x^2 - 3x - 18 &= 0 \\\\   x^2 - x - 6 &= 0 \\end{aligned}
[2] Coefficients a, b, c
    │ a = 1, \\quad b = -1, \\quad c = -6
[3] Discriminant : Δ > 0
    │ \\Delta = b^2 - 4ac = \\left(-1\\right)^2 - 4 \\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\cdot \\left(-6\\right) = 25
[4] Formule du second degré
    │ \\begin{aligned}   x &= \\dfrac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{\\Delta}}{2a} \\\\   &= \\dfrac{-\\left(-1\\right) \\pm \\sqrt{25}}{2 \\cdot \\left(1\\right)} \\end{aligned}
[5] Simplification
    │ \\begin{aligned}   x_1 &= \\dfrac{1 - \\sqrt{25}}{2 1} = -2 \\\\
  x_2 &= \\dfrac{1 + \\sqrt{25}}{2 1} = 3 \\end{aligned}
[6] Ensemble des solutions
    │ S = \\left\\{ -2 \\,;\\, 3 \\right\\}
"
`;

